comments.body:
@julianoes The QNH calibration is to adjust the pressure-to-altitude conversion according to local weather conditions. It does not affect the absolute pressure value. My goal was not to get the altitude based on pressure but to get a relative height difference between ground station and drone. So I am using absolute pressure values on both ends. 
But indeed acording to specs pressure sensors can have a tolerance of +/-10m.

Yes it would be good to be able to activate set_rate_scaled_pressure() by a parameter. The pressure value from mavsdk.telemetry cannot be used without the PX4 streaming this value. And to those only using the mavsdk without detailled knowledge of mavlink, a parameter would be more conveniant..

